{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/404103-questions-about-obfuscate","id":404103,"title":"Questions about Obfuscate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-12T22:02:36-08:00","id":404103,"title":"Questions about Obfuscate","content":"<br /> 1) Someone uses Obfuscate in your presence. Do you know they did something? Did they &quot;disappear&quot;? Do you not notice they're gone?<br /> <br /> 1b) What if you are directly interacting with them? I.e. they do it mid conversation or mid combat.<br /> <br /> 2) Can you use Obfuscate 1 to cloak your Predatory Aura and nothing else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T03:31:30-08:00","id":404351,"title":"","content":"1. What level are we talking about? Level 1 it automatically fails against someone they are actively engaged with for any reason and creates an opposed perception check penalized by the user's Obfuscate rating for onlookers. Level 2 they get an opposed perception check penalized by the user's Obfuscate score if its used on something or someone (at level 3+) the person is aware of but not necessarily using or talking to. If they're actively engaged in using (ie like trying to use it on the gun they have pointed at the Obfuscate user though honestly why they'd let the person touch the gun in such a scenario is beyond me.) the object then I would say it's an auto-fail. Obfuscate doesn't unilaterally require Auspex, Tenure, or a Supernatural detection ability like Kenning to potentially see through it any more. <br /> <br /> 1b Automatic auto fail against the person being attacked or talking to the person. It's right there in the book saying the person (or people) being engaged is immune to the other person's Obfuscate. Onlookers get the standard modified perception check.<br /> <br /> 2. Yes, but it's subject to the Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T08:15:37-08:00","id":404481,"title":"","content":"You know how Batman occasionally &quot;disappears&quot; into the night in the middle of a conversation? It's kind of like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:59:17-07:00","id":463758,"title":"","content":"I've been bad about asking questions that already exist before:<br /> <br /> Say my Nosferatu, Layla, has Obfuscate 3. She's promised her buddy, Charles, that she'll free him from the captivity of the local Ordo Dracul/Invictus court that's putting him on trial. Can she, in the middle of the trial, walk in and grab him while everybody's there and paying attention to him, or will she have to do something trickier than that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T13:39:47-07:00","id":463838,"title":"","content":"I think she could do it, but a lot of vampires would probably start lashing out and activating auspex. Having the doors locked.<br /> <br /> I've never had a situation like that but in the last game while the coterie was talking to a vampire who claimed she was being hunted, a vampire walked into the bar and, upon seeing them, just seemed to blink out of existence. It really got them on edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-31-2015, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:14:31-07:00","id":463861,"title":"","content":"You'd probably want Obfuscate 3 for yourself and Obfuscate 2+3 for the target. Form there, it depends on what the ST wants. If it's a quick one and done and the ST wants to move the story along, that will get through most but not all defenses. Lashing Out does nothing, but Auspex is definitely a thing. In addition, since the vampire disappeared, it's reasonable to lock the facility down. Someone with the Staff merit should be able to find the vampires within Wits + Stealth + Obfuscate minutes from the point of <i>entry </i>to get back out, or you can just make one roll based on the NPCs to track the PC depending on feel. Safe Place can hinder rolls to travel and navigate through the area and pick its locks. Note that since the person is on a time crunch, autopicking is not an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:21:48-07:00","id":463871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/404103-questions-about-obfuscate?p=463758#post463758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been bad about asking questions that already exist before:<br /> <br /> Say my Nosferatu, Layla, has Obfuscate 3. She's promised her buddy, Charles, that she'll free him from the captivity of the local Ordo Dracul/Invictus court that's putting him on trial. Can she, in the middle of the trial, walk in and grab him while everybody's there and paying attention to him, or will she have to do something trickier than that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Layla can use Cloak of Night when she activates Face in the Crowd to make herself completely unnoticeable, walk right up to Charles in the middle of the trial without being seen. She can then use Cloak of Night with Touch of Shadow, allowing her to use it on a person (in this case, Charles) instead of an object or animal. However, Touch of Shadow only makes the affected object (or person, in this case) not stand out, it doesn't gain the additional concealment from Cloak of Night that Face in the Crowd does. Observers subconsciously register the presence of someone or something under the affect of Touch of Shadow, but don't consciously pay attention to it, unless they are forced to interact with it in some way. Now, I'm not sure if being on trial counts for that or not, but I would at least allow the court to roll Wits + Composure - Layla's Obfuscate to notice the occluded object as usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:34:01-07:00","id":463885,"title":"","content":"'If another vampire manages to perceive him, through Auspex, attack, or any other means, she can sense his predatory aura and lash out. If she wins the predatory aura contest, Cloak of Night shatters, as does any other use of Obfuscate the vampire made.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:46:16-07:00","id":463900,"title":"","content":"@Nofather: Is that a quote? If yes, from where?<br /> <br /> @Charlaquin: You can use Touch of Shadow + Cloak of the Night to make someone else vanish entirely by spending two Vitae. &quot;The vampire can also spend an extra point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd <i>or Touch of Shadow </i>to vanish completely. Rather than being overlooked or just an \u201caverage presence,\u201d the vampire instead completely disappears.&quot; (emphasis mine).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:53:33-07:00","id":463906,"title":"","content":"It's from <i>Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle</i>, in the section on the Cloak of Night discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T14:55:43-07:00","id":463908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/404103-questions-about-obfuscate?p=463900#post463900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Charlaquin: You can use Touch of Shadow + Cloak of the Night to make someone else vanish entirely by spending two Vitae. &quot;The vampire can also spend an extra point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd <b><i>or Touch of Shadow </i></b>to vanish completely. Rather than being overlooked or just an \u201caverage presence,\u201d the vampire instead completely disappears.&quot; (emphasis mine).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what book you are reading, but the italicized part is not written in mine. You might want to check yours again.<br /> <br /> EDIT: So quoting apparently italicizes the whole block of text... so I bolded the part that's not in my book instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-31-2015, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T02:13:58-07:00","id":464423,"title":"","content":"You can't make other people vanish completely with basic applications of Obfuscate. You need Cloak the Gathering Devotion for that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T07:09:24-07:00","id":464647,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers and help everyone. In the scenario described, my Nosferatu Layla is actually a NPC, the Court is most of the player characters, and Charles is one of the PCs who has been caught Diablerizing their enemies and violating the First Tradition. During his captivity, he's been in touch with Layla through Blood Sorcery (Cruac to summon rat messengers, Animalism to send messages).<br /> <br /> Layla and Charles have been planning to bust him out during the Trial. It seems like Layla will have to cause a significant distraction, make use of Nightmare, and call in her Gangrel buddy to run crowd control. Should be an exciting session.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/404103-questions-about-obfuscate?p=463900#post463900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Nofather: Is that a quote? If yes, from where?<br /> <br /> @Charlaquin: You can use Touch of Shadow + Cloak of the Night to make someone else vanish entirely by spending two Vitae. &quot;The vampire can also spend an extra point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd <i>or Touch of Shadow </i>to vanish completely. Rather than being overlooked or just an \u201caverage presence,\u201d the vampire instead completely disappears.&quot; (emphasis mine).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm also not seeing the <i>or Touch of Shadow</i> part in either my <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i> hard copy or my <i>Vampire: The Requiem 2nd Edition</i> PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}